      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "VESTA BALE (7) was a winner two back when prominent throughout then got further back last time and could manage only a 3.5 lengths 5th at Sale (24.97). Looks the one to beat on her best form. PAW AMALFI (4) flew the lids off the inside draw with a fast early split and gave a sight, finishing a 0.8 lengths second (30.70) over 525m at this track. Expected to be in the finish again. GREYSYND BONNIE (6) struggled in tougher grade last start after drifting back at Traralgon, but prior to that won by 2 lengths at Bendigo (28.39) beating Paw Nevada in a Bottom Up - Grade 5 on July 22. Can figure in the finish. PAW NITRO (1) missed the placings here last start but is well-placed to bounce back.",
